+**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
+*   **Resolution Mismatch:** If one point cloud is significantly denser than the other, the term corresponding to the denser cloud will dominate the average if not normalized by cardinality, though the standard formula normalizes by $|P|$ and $|Q|$ separately. However, if $|P| \neq |Q|$, the sampling strategy must be consistent to avoid bias [S9].
+*   **Topology Errors:** CD is sensitive to outliers. A single large protrusion can significantly increase the distance from the ground truth to the prediction, even if the overall shape is correct [S11].
+*   **Alignment:** CD assumes the point clouds are in the same coordinate frame. Misalignment leads to artificially high distances. ICP registration is often required [S6].
